@*
 * FILE ROLE: Home index view — default landing page rendered by HomeController.Index()
 *            via return View() with no model. Demonstrates a ViewResult with no typed
 *            model: the view accesses only ViewData set by the controller or the
 *            view's own @{} block.
 *
 * KEY CONCEPTS DEMONSTRATED:
 *   return View()
 *     The controller calls View() with no arguments. MVC resolves the view file by
 *     convention: Views/{ControllerName}/{ActionName}.cshtml → Views/Home/Index.cshtml.
 *     No @model directive is used because the controller passes no model object.
 *
 *   Layout = "_Layout"
 *     Tells the view engine to wrap this view's output in Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml.
 *     Without this (or a _ViewStart.cshtml setting the default), no layout is applied.
 *
 *   ViewData["Title"]
 *     Set here in the view's @{} block; read in _Layout.cshtml's <title> element.
 *     The layout processes AFTER the view's @{} block runs, so this value is available.
 *
 * COVERED IN DETAIL LATER → 03. Views & Razor Syntax
 *@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

